// Book · E Comments: every comment of the code, one entry a code, written once. The code carries only the code (// E12); 4. COMMENTS shows them, 5. MASTER ties each to its code, laws and citations. Edit here only.
BOOK("comments", {
 "E1": {"text": "First Keep v100 · the world reads its numbers from the Books (books/*.js), never from here: one home each."},
 "E2": {"text": "A Book entry is { key, value, name, cite, law } under its code; the game sees each book as one object by key (D, A, C, W, G), and a shell's slot points at a code (D53, D86.walk)."},
 "E3": {"text": "every code in every book"},
 "E4": {"text": "a slot's pointer, read"},
 "E5": {"text": "S the shells (books/shells.js): a row names its layer, ticks its capabilities (SC) and points each slot at a book. has() is the one way the code asks what a thing can do."},
 "E6": {"text": "The frames (QBD). The grid is square in its own frame; the board frame is the grid turned A1 about the site's middle; the view foreshortens depth by sin A2 and shows height by cos A2."},
 "E7": {"text": "QBE: the most a tile may step up or down over its own width and still be a slope"},
 "E8": {"text": "QBK the art frame: a building is painted with its front along x and sheared by SKEW so that edge follows the grid; its depth is ART_T a unit of width, the back standing ART_S of that to the right"},
 "E9": {"text": "QBF the dice (N65): one seed, Mulberry32. Every roll names Who, What, Where, When, Why and How beside it (L13)."},
 "E10": {"text": "two streams from the map's seed, dealt fresh at makeUnits: the rules' (M1), so the same seed plays the same game, and the looks' (D187), so a look never shifts a rule roll"},
 "E11": {"text": "QAZ a fractal line (N60): K waves, the k-th of amplitude k^(−H), H = 2 − Dim; a coast's Dim is about 1.25. Returns a function of the way along, in radians, giving −1 to 1."},
 "E12": {"text": "QAZ as a surface: K plane waves in rolled directions, the same amplitudes; scale is the longest wave in units. Returns a function of (x, y) giving about −1 to 1."},
 "E13": {"text": "The coast (L2 Cut at the board's edge; L4 Edge). Where it stands out it is a headland and a cliff, where it bends in a bay and a beach (QBG)."},
 "E14": {"text": "The roll: Who the map · What how far the coast wanders in and out · Where the coast only; within D5 of every corner the same wander (L12), free along the middle of each side · When the map is made · Why no two maps share a coast, and every home gets the same one · How QAZ on the dice."},
 "E15": {"text": "pos: the way along the side from its start; returns [wander, cliffness]"},
 "E16": {"text": "−1 bay to 1 headland"},
 "E17": {"text": "The ground: one height a tile. Depth is the way in from the coast (negative at sea). Land stands at D13; a beach falls to the water over D16, a cliff over D17 (L4); the sea deepens with distance. The stratum a tile shows is whichever its height reaches (L1)."},
 "E18": {"text": "height, depth from the coast, the four drawn corner heights, the forest floor"},
 "E19": {"text": "marsh (TW1): always wet (KI1)"},
 "E20": {"text": "the way in from the coast at a board point, and the coast's cliffness there"},
 "E21": {"text": "the drawn corners (QBE): at every grid corner the tiles round it are sorted by height and split where a step passes the angle of repose; each group shares one height, so a slope meets without a crack and a face stands where it should"},
 "E22": {"text": "Floor 2, terrain (layer 90): every piece is a Cut or a Raise on the one height field (L2, L3); the layer that shows follows (L1), a step past the angle of repose is a face (QBE)."},
 "E23": {"text": "a spot in a corner's own frame (u along one edge, v along the other), the same in all four (L12)"},
 "E24": {"text": "the four roads: corner to middle"},
 "E25": {"text": "every tile whose middle lies within r of a board point: fn(k, d, dx, dy)"},
 "E26": {"text": "a lake: a bowl (deep at the middle, D27) inside a fractal shore (QAZ, D28); where the land stands out into it the shore is a face, where it bends back a bank (QBG); a lake's bank falls over D32, the sea's beach over D16 (L4)"},
 "E27": {"text": "a wandering line (QAZ) from a to b, pinned at both ends; null when any point fails ok"},
 "E28": {"text": "a channel: discs along a line; w the half-width, deep the bed; the bank falls over D32"},
 "E29": {"text": "a smooth hill: its steepest slope is 0.77 h / r, under the angle of repose at these numbers"},
 "E30": {"text": "The home pond: Who every corner · What one small lake · Where Z3, the same spot in each corner's own frame (D51, D52, L12) · When the map is made · Why a home has water to fish and to sail, and the same water for all · How one shore rolled once (QAZ), shared"},
 "E31": {"text": "Lakes: Who the map · What their number, size and place · Where Z4, off the roads and the middle, inside the play edge · When the map is made · Why no two maps share their water · How a count between D25, sizes on the power law of lakes (QBA, Pareto draw), places uniform, each shore QAZ"},
 "E32": {"text": "Rivers: Who the map · What one from each lake big enough, to the nearest free coast · Where Z4 only; a river never enters a home (L12) · When the map is made · Why water that moves, a way to sail out, a line to hold · How the path wanders (QAZ), the width grows with the lake (QBB)"},
 "E33": {"text": "Fords (TC4): Who every river · What a shallow crossing · Where wherever a river crosses one of the four roads, and once more at a rolled spot · When with the river · Why towns grew at fords: a road meets water where it can be waded · How the bed raised to wading depth over D33"},
 "E34": {"text": "Hills (TR1): Who the map · What a few smooth rises · Where Z4, clear of water and roads · When the map is made · Why high ground to hold and to see from · How count D36, radius D37, a dome of D38"},
 "E35": {"text": "Streams (TC3): Who each hill · What a thin, wadeable run to the nearest lake · Where Z4 · When with the hills · Why water springs where ground rises · How a channel of D34 by D35"},
 "E36": {"text": "Rock (TR2): Who the map · What outcrops nothing walks over or through · Where Z4, on dry land, off the roads · When the map is made · Why cover and chokepoints inland · How count D39, radius D40, raised D41 in one step so every edge is a face (QBE); its top is bare (D23)"},
 "E37": {"text": "Crevices (TC5): Who the map · What a dry trench nothing crosses · Where Z4, off the roads and water · When the map is made · Why a line that cannot be walked, without water · How count D42, a wandering line of D45, cut to D44 so both walls are faces"},
 "E38": {"text": "Forest (TF1): Who the map · What where the trees grow (the trees themselves come on floor 3) · Where a wall round every home at D50 with the road through it (the same for all, L12), and patches over Z4 by a rolled surface; never on water, slopes or roads · When the map is made · Why woods to cut, to hide in, to go round · How QAZ as a surface, scale D48, standing where it rises past D49"},
 "E39": {"text": "the wood's edge keeps one tile from any slope or water"},
 "E40": {"text": "Floor 3, non-movables (layer 100): shells with no Walk, an Amount and a Yield (S). Each stands on one flat tile of land; a big one takes the tiles under it. Nothing here moves; floor 5 takes from the amounts."},
 "E41": {"text": "the finds (layer 100), from their shells: kind → code, yield, amount, the ground kept clear"},
 "E42": {"text": "QBJ Z1's store, from what the first age up costs (D129, Mid's Bronze; Albert's rule): food for the age and the villagers, wood for the mill, the lumber camp, the homes and the barracks, each with a margin (D62–D69)"},
 "E43": {"text": "what stands on each tile, and the shells themselves"},
 "E44": {"text": "the free tile nearest a spot"},
 "E45": {"text": "a shell on a tile; its stand wanders within the tile by D82 on the dice, so no wood is a grid"},
 "E46": {"text": "the n free tiles nearest a spot: a grove (marked as woods, the trees follow) or a berry patch"},
 "E47": {"text": "The home finds: Who every corner · What Z1's berries, grove, gold and stone, sized by QBJ; Z3's the same at D72 times, with iron · Where fixed spots in the corner's frame (D70, D71), the same in all four (L12) · When the map is made · Why every player starts with the same ground and the same means to the next age · How one home dice (QBF), restarted at each corner, so the four are alike to the stand of each bush"},
 "E48": {"text": "Z4's finds: Who the map · What piles of gold, stone and iron, berry patches, and the gifts: ruins, cemeteries, campfires, treasure · Where Z4, on flat free land, off the roads, the middle and the play edge · When the map is made · Why the game beyond the homestead is to be found, not known · How counts D73–D81, places uniform until one is clear, each a roll"},
 "E49": {"text": "The trees: Who every tile of woods (TF1, and the groves) · What one tree, its stand, size and shade · Where its tile · When the map is made · Why the woods are what is cut for wood (R1) · How three rolls a tile"},
 "E50": {"text": "drawn back to front"},
 "E51": {"text": "a tree with trees on all eight sides is deep: nothing can stand between it and its neighbours, so the deep woods are painted once a chunk (see the woods cache)"},
 "E52": {"text": "0 water, 1 sand, 2 dirt, 3 grass; bare dirt again high over the land (D23)"},
 "E53": {"text": "the first band is what can be waded (D24)"},
 "E54": {"text": "the forest floor: the grass, shaded; the marsh: the grass, toward the water"},
 "E55": {"text": "what a face shows between two heights (L1): the grass is the land's top skin; anything raised above it shows bare earth"},
 "E56": {"text": "Drawn once in the view frame: every tile a lifted quad, a face where it steps down toward the camera. Then every frame is one picture, moved and scaled."},
 "E57": {"text": "the masks at a quarter scale: the land in white and in shadow, the inland water"},
 "E58": {"text": "a quad a, b, c, d (top-left round to bottom-left on the screen) grown half a pixel right and down, so the next tile's edge lands on solid paint and no seam shows"},
 "E59": {"text": "the grass's blades: one 64-unit tile of short strokes in two tints of C4, repeated (preview 49's)"},
 "E60": {"text": "the light stands high to the left and in front: ground leaning that way is lit, ground leaning away is shaded, 3% a unit of lean over a tile"},
 "E61": {"text": "runs: flat tiles of one colour in a row drawn as one quad (no seams, few fills)"},
 "E62": {"text": "faces: the +y edge and the +x edge face the camera (the turn is under 45°)"},
 "E63": {"text": "The view (layer 140): one camera, drag to pan, pinch or wheel to zoom; the overlays are drawn each frame over the one picture."},
 "E64": {"text": "one flag a layer code (the panel, floor 8) and Fast"},
 "E65": {"text": "The door (floor 8): the modules (menu, econ, combat, ai) hang on these hooks and read the world through FK; nothing else of theirs touches this file"},
 "E66": {"text": "event: a named happening (a blow, a drop, a raise) that the sound and the feel answer, by the names in books/sound.js HE1"},
 "E67": {"text": "a slow beat's turn (D182–D184): the step whose seconds played cross it, its phase in Mid's frames (D98)"},
 "E68": {"text": "the screen jolts with a heavy impact (QBT)"},
 "E69": {"text": "the walking grid, at the land's height, clipped to the played ground: the coast's line brought D7 in (L6)"},
 "E70": {"text": "Z1 to Z4 from each corner (D3 to D6), at the land's height (L11: a rule drawn on the ground, not ground)"},
 "E71": {"text": "The brushes (preview 49, 18-figures.js): a polygon, an ellipse, a line, two gradients; g is the canvas being painted"},
 "E72": {"text": "The building art (preview 49, 19-building-art.js; Nov 3, the last build before the camera turn): every piece drawn from its own point lists, in units, feet at (0, 0), the front edge along x, the back up and to the right. A building's level and its research footing are skins (PB3, PB4, PB6, PB12); civs, seasons and flags are cut."},
 "E73": {"text": "a building picture's height, from its look"},
 "E74": {"text": "The node art (the same file): six trees, three bushes, stone, gold and iron; r is a dice for the leaf blobs"},
 "E75": {"text": "The figures (preview 49, 18-figures.js): people and beasts drawn from data, feet at (0, 0), facing right, a person about 21 tall; fr 0–3 the walk, 10 and up at work (the tool, two poses). One look a code; the soldiers' looks are Mid's own (F18), the rest of the roster stays in preview 49 as skins."},
 "E76": {"text": "the brushes: one drawing routine a shape; a look in books/sprites.js names its brush and the brush's settings ($side the owner's colour, $side*0.6 a tint of it, any colour*0.6 a tint of that)"},
 "E77": {"text": "a figure's frame, from its look"},
 "E78": {"text": "B the buildings (layer 110; shells without Walk): the size in tiles (D8–D11; a wall piece is one tile, D12), Open or Closed (S Styles), the picture it wears. Health, prices and times come with the Content pull."},
 "E79": {"text": "the buildings (layer 110), from their shells: name, size in tiles, Open, the picture, what it takes in"},
 "E80": {"text": "a building stands on n × n flat free tiles from (i, j); Closed takes them (OCC 2), Open leaves them walkable (OCC 3)"},
 "E81": {"text": "The Town Center: Who every corner · What one · Where Z2 on the road at D84, the same in all four (L12) · When the map is made · Why the game starts with a hall to gather at · How no roll: fixed"},
 "E82": {"text": "Floor 5, movables (layer 120): U units and M moveables are shells that walk. Each stands at a board point, walks tile to tile along a path (QBL), and does one thing at a time."},
 "E83": {"text": "one a corner (C5–C8); the player is 0"},
 "E84": {"text": "the units and moveables (layer 120), from their shells: name, look, pace (a D86 key)"},
 "E85": {"text": "the tool a villager works a find with (WORKTOOL): axe, hands, pick, from the Sprites book (PN1 tool), the one home econ.js reads"},
 "E86": {"text": "walking (L5, top rules): land or a ford is walked; a thing, a closed building or a step past the angle of repose is not"},
 "E87": {"text": "inland water bearing ice (QQ): walked as if flat"},
 "E88": {"text": "the pace's books (QCB): its states and Pandolf's coefficients (D224), the friction a step needs (G9), slipping (G10); the player's side, told when its people slip"},
 "E89": {"text": "QBL A* over the tiles, the eight ways of D198, straight 1 and diagonal √2, the heuristic the octile distance (N74). goal(k) says when a tile will do; returns the tiles to walk, or null"},
 "E90": {"text": "most: the tiles it may open before giving up"},
 "E91": {"text": "no cutting a corner"},
 "E92": {"text": "a unit on a tile; its stand wanders in the tile (D82)"},
 "E93": {"text": "a path of one tile (already there) walks to its middle: no step past the end"},
 "E94": {"text": "to a tile"},
 "E95": {"text": "to a tile beside one"},
 "E96": {"text": "the drop-off for a yield: the side's nearest building that takes it in (SC Drop-off, B's fifth field)"},
 "E97": {"text": "to a tile along a building's edge (the ring of tiles round it, byB)"},
 "E98": {"text": "a find used up is gone; its tile is free again"},
 "E99": {"text": "one tick for every unit"},
 "E100": {"text": "walking: toward the next point at the walker's pace (QCB) over the ground it steps onto; true when it gets there"},
 "E101": {"text": "metres walked, which turn the stride (QBU); its speed now, which a blow carries (QBT)"},
 "E102": {"text": "wildlife wanders: after a Poisson wait (QM, mean D94) it walks to a free tile within D95"},
 "E103": {"text": "M3 the grids (a spatial hash): units by squares of D185, refiled after each step's walking, buildings by D186; a new unit is filed as it comes. A search looks only nearby"},
 "E104": {"text": "every unit within r of from (a square), never itself"},
 "E105": {"text": "the buildings within r of (x, y) by their squares, a little beyond on the edges; refiled when one comes or goes (Mid's rule); stops when fn says true"},
 "E106": {"text": "the rules' dice and the looks', from the map's seed but not its stream"},
 "E107": {"text": "The villagers: Who every side · What D67 villagers · Where round its Town Center · When the game starts · Why hands to gather and build · How the free tiles nearest the hall"},
 "E108": {"text": "The wildlife: Who the map · What herds of deer and packs of wolves · Where Z4, on walkable ground · When the map is made · Why food to hunt, teeth to fear · How counts D90–D93, places uniform until one walks"},
 "E109": {"text": "which walkers, how many groups and how big: the book's (D181)"},
 "E110": {"text": "what carries a walker: its mount, else its own body (W)"},
 "E111": {"text": "The body's laws (Book 1): mass from what a shell is made of (W), the blow that sends a body off (QBT), the slide to rest on the ground under it (G), the sway of the wounded (QBS)"},
 "E112": {"text": "QBT: the whole striker when it moves, else its weapon; the struck one is sent off at v = m·v ÷ (m + M)"},
 "E113": {"text": "QBT: friction slows it by μ g a second until it rests; anything it cannot stand on stops it"},
 "E114": {"text": "the mean speed over the step, so the slide ends where v² ÷ 2μg says"},
 "E115": {"text": "QBS: none while the body holds (classes I, II); grows over class III to the tipping angle; there in class IV. Its rhythm the body's pendulum"},
 "E116": {"text": "a unit's picture: its look at its frame, its rank and its side's armour kit, facing right, painted once per look, colour, rank, kit and frame (LOOKBOX gives the box); a look marked elite carries the gold pennant at a rank (Mid's sprite)"},
 "E117": {"text": "The things, drawn each frame back to front, only those on the screen. A picture is painted once per look and zoom step, then stamped (the sprite cache); far out (D83) a node is a dot. The gifts are drawn direct, as tints of C."},
 "E118": {"text": "W × H units, the art's origin at (tx, ty), its anchor (the point stamped at the thing's stand) at (ax, ay)"},
 "E119": {"text": "the node art's own small dice, seeded by the variant, so a tree's leaves fall the same each paint"},
 "E120": {"text": "each drawn at its stand (x, y on the screen), s pixels a unit"},
 "E121": {"text": "a find far out, from its look"},
 "E122": {"text": "Floor 6, climate (layer 130): one sky over the whole board (185 m across: one weather), acting on everything below (L7). The clock is Y: a day D20, a season D21, a year D22."},
 "E123": {"text": "QA the sun: sin a = sin φ sin δ + cos φ cos δ cos H; φ D99, δ swings ±23.44° over the year from the spring equinox, H turns with the day (noon at the day's middle)"},
 "E124": {"text": "light by the sun's height, the twilights at −6, −12, −18 (SoRen's ramp, QD)"},
 "E125": {"text": "QP the one first-order lag, x to its level L over τ: x(t) = L + (x0 − L) e^(−t/τ) (N16; Mid's relax: wetness here, and the market, nerve, healing, loyalty to come)"},
 "E126": {"text": "QH the rain: a two-state chain, drawn once a game hour (a day's 24th): P(wet | dry) and P(wet | wet) are D102; a wet spell draws its intensity and the wind's sign once, from the rules' dice (QCL), a storm from D103. Snow falls instead when the air is at or under 1 °C (QI)"},
 "E127": {"text": "the season's mean, eased into the next"},
 "E128": {"text": "what falls"},
 "E129": {"text": "rain and snow come and go over tens of seconds (SoRen), toward the spell's intensity"},
 "E130": {"text": "QP settle: wet in D104, dry in D105"},
 "E131": {"text": "QO degree-day melt, rain on snow twice as fast"},
 "E132": {"text": "QQ: lake ice grows with the freezing degree-seconds and bears at D109; ice on the ground grows the same way while the ground is wet, full at D225"},
 "E133": {"text": "QM: fog comes on a Poisson wait (D110) and stays D111"},
 "E134": {"text": "fog, or mist after rain at dawn and dusk (KW8)"},
 "E135": {"text": "QL, QM: strikes on Poisson waits in a storm"},
 "E136": {"text": "a strike: on the ground in view when close, a sheet flash when far; the flash never comes within D112 of the last (QL, WCAG 2.3.1), and the bolt is pinned to the ground it hits"},
 "E137": {"text": "a far flash: its thunder from beyond the screen"},
 "E138": {"text": "the rain's fall speed (QJ, Atlas's fit to Gunn & Kinzer); how many of the pool are falling: the strength"},
 "E139": {"text": "on the ground, under everything: snow whitens the land (screen), wet darkens it (multiply), ice whitens the inland water"},
 "E140": {"text": "over everything: what falls, the strikes, the flash, the night, the white of low visibility and the fog"},
 "E141": {"text": "SoRen's bolt: a channel from the top of the sky to the ground with a fork or two, three strokes from a soft glow to a bright core; its foot lights the ground round it"},
 "E142": {"text": "the channel wanders but leans home to its foot"},
 "E143": {"text": "the light: the sun's by the ramp, clouds take a quarter, the horizon's warmth within 8° of it"},
 "E144": {"text": "KW7: Koschmieder's reach (QK) limits sight on the Display floor; here the haze"},
 "E145": {"text": "Marsh (TW1): Who the map · What a wet margin round a lake or two · Where Z4's lakes, the land D115 out from the water · When the map is made · Why ground that is always mud (KI2), slow to cross, never built on · How count D114, lakes picked by the dice"},
 "E146": {"text": "Floor 7, display (layer 140): what the player sees. The fog of war: every tile is unseen, seen once, or in sight now (the player's units see D117, its buildings further; fog in the air shortens sight, QK); the unseen is dark, the remembered dim (D118). Shadows fall from the sun (QAT)."},
 "E147": {"text": "the player's sight, every D119: what was in sight is remembered; what the units and buildings of side 0 reach now is seen, never past the visibility (QK)"},
 "E148": {"text": "the sea is never fogged"},
 "E149": {"text": "the fog image is one tile a pixel in the grid's frame; one affine lays it on the ground (QBD): the turn, the tilt and the camera together"},
 "E150": {"text": "QAT the shadow: length = height × cot(the sun's height), capped at D120 heights, thrown away from the sun; the sun rises on the right, stands over the bottom of the screen at noon (the camera looks north), sets on the left"},
 "E151": {"text": "left at sunrise, up at noon, right at sunset"},
 "E152": {"text": "under the buildings and units: a building's footprint thrown by its height, a unit's foot by its own; none under the trees (the woods are their own shade)"},
 "E153": {"text": "the box's shadow: its top thrown, joined to its foot along every edge, one fill so the overlaps stay one shade"},
 "E154": {"text": "The woods cache: the deep trees (eight tree neighbours) are painted once per chunk of the board and zoom step; the rest of the things are stamped each frame. Cutting a tree wakes its neighbours and repaints the chunk."},
 "E155": {"text": "chunks of CS × CS tiles"},
 "E156": {"text": "a tree cut: its chunk is stale, and its neighbours stand at an edge now"},
 "E157": {"text": "each chunk's box in the view frame, with room above for the trees' height"},
 "E158": {"text": "the chunk's deep trees on one canvas"},
 "E159": {"text": "a hit moves to the back: the oldest goes first"},
 "E160": {"text": "a wounded one sways about its feet (QBS)"},
 "E161": {"text": "L6 the play edge: the line between tiles D7 in from the coast and the rest, along the tiles' own edges"},
 "E162": {"text": "Touch: one finger pans, two pinch; a wheel zooms about the pointer; a held finger picks more, drags the crosshair or draws a box (F21)."},
 "E163": {"text": "the camera rule: the board never leaves the screen's middle; a board smaller than the screen sits centred"},
 "E164": {"text": "what is under the finger: the tile at the land's height and the nearest unit it may see (yours, or one in sight and not hidden), within the larger of D246 hit and hitZ a zoom (Mid's hitAt); the menu answers the tap"},
 "E165": {"text": "The seed of the day (QBF): the date as YYYYMMDD, the same map for everyone that day; a seed in the address overrides it."},
 "E166": {"text": "the door: what the modules may touch"},
 "E167": {"text": "the test hook"},
 "E168": {"text": "First Keep v100 · menu.js (floor 8): everything on the glass. Lives alone; it reads the world through one function, read(), and acts through one, act(verb, arg), backed by VERBS, where every verb carries its own whyNot. A dim button never runs: it says why."},
 "E169": {"text": "Its shape lives in the Screen book (books/screen.js): the mold, the Build tabs, the card's rows and the subject's ticks that pick them, the pages and which are Tall. Nothing of it is typed here."},
 "E170": {"text": "its numbers live in books/measure.js (D); nothing is typed here"},
 "E171": {"text": "the codes and their floors; Lock is a mark for us (no floor is locked yet)"},
 "E172": {"text": "the Screen book: the Build tabs are its; a building shows priced once econ prices it, else Later"},
 "E173": {"text": "the seat, and who it trains first: asked of the books, never named"},
 "E174": {"text": "the classes War's Train box offers (D133), each as the first kind of it open at this age (Mid's kindOf)"},
 "E175": {"text": "a page that keeps its own height (SC20)"},
 "E176": {"text": "the new game's choices: the first is the label's row in Albert's template; built ones set the game, the rest wait (dim, they say why)"},
 "E177": {"text": "which choices are floors yet"},
 "E178": {"text": "the base's columns, Albert's template"},
 "E179": {"text": "the base's icons: one 24-unit box each, line icons in the cell's colour, finds in their own"},
 "E180": {"text": "the resources in their colours (COLORS.md)"},
 "E181": {"text": "the colours: COLORS.md, one name each, set once on :root; nothing below uses a colour that is not here (the map's own paint excepted)"},
 "E182": {"text": "the glass's own state, nothing of the world's"},
 "E183": {"text": "60w 60f, as Albert's Build menu"},
 "E184": {"text": "read: the one window onto the world the glass draws from"},
 "E185": {"text": "VERBS: every way the player may act, each with its reason not to. act() asks whyNot first; a reason stops it and is said"},
 "E186": {"text": "Train a kind: the nearest finished building that trains it; a kind before its age says which age it waits for"},
 "E187": {"text": "a channel's volume, a step a tap (HX10)"},
 "E188": {"text": "sound on or off"},
 "E189": {"text": "a cell for what is drawn but not yet built: Albert's reminder"},
 "E190": {"text": "the new game: the bell (D134), fog, the day's map or a fresh one"},
 "E191": {"text": "tap a yield: new villagers go there (the ring)"},
 "E192": {"text": "tap picks, slide places the ghost, tap again builds"},
 "E193": {"text": "the cells: one mold; a verb's cell is dim when its whyNot says so, and a dim cell only says why"},
 "E194": {"text": "a cell's object arguments live here by key, since the DOM holds strings"},
 "E195": {"text": "the mold: a ribbon is an optional label and a strip of n equal cells; seg puts them in one frame with one lit. Every screen is a list of ribbons"},
 "E196": {"text": "the mold: every screen is rows on one six-column grid (the Formation). A row holds cells and parts; a part is an optional label and a strip of choices, seg puts them in one frame with one lit"},
 "E197": {"text": "Albert's Town Center: the bars in the title, three tabs, the queue, train, tech"},
 "E198": {"text": "Fast and New sit in the title row; the volumes add a row, so the Yard ticks Tall (SN13)"},
 "E199": {"text": "one row a name in SN4; each answers for the subject t, or says nothing"},
 "E200": {"text": "the base: Albert's template. Corners Yard and War; who works where; Build and − + under each yield"},
 "E201": {"text": "war mode: Albert's War rows. Left the people's orders, the middle box (map, squads and their dials, orders, kinds), right the army's"},
 "E202": {"text": "the top bar: Albert's two ribbons. The stores, sound, play, mail; the age, the clock, people, idle, records, rank, army"},
 "E203": {"text": "Relations and Misfits: one row a people: who and where they stand, (a bribe for misfits), the three stances, ✓. Drawn now, built with diplomacy (Later)"},
 "E204": {"text": "the five stores, sound, play, mail (SN5)"},
 "E205": {"text": "a page opens from the bottom edge, over the base's rows; the card waits behind it"},
 "E206": {"text": "the ghost: press and slide on the map moves it; the tile under the finger is its middle. Build confirms. Nothing of this reaches the canvas's own pan while a ghost is up"},
 "E207": {"text": "the tap: the glass answers first. A ghost takes it; aiming takes it; a unit or a thing under it becomes the subject, and a picked villager or soldier is sent at it"},
 "E208": {"text": "one height for every page but the Tall ones: each is laid out once, the tallest sets the panel, the others fill it (Albert: menus never move)"},
 "E209": {"text": "the tallest of the pages that are not Tall sets the one height"},
 "E210": {"text": "sized once the modules and fonts are in (the first start)"},
 "E211": {"text": "the game opens on the player's hall"},
 "E212": {"text": "the version, said once (D171)"},
 "E213": {"text": "First Keep v100 · econ.js (floor 9): the economy. Lives alone; touches the world only through FK. Costs, homes, training, sites, ages, upkeep, and the villager as one state machine: idle, walk, gather, carry, build, repair, wait."},
 "E214": {"text": "seconds played, and when the bell rings"},
 "E215": {"text": "gone: marked when it leaves the map (below)"},
 "E216": {"text": "paying: a side pays all of a cost or none of it (SB Cost)"},
 "E217": {"text": "a site: a building paid for and placed at done 0; villagers raise it. canPlace mirrors build's rule without building"},
 "E218": {"text": "training, research and the age: one queue at the building, as long as the mold's six and what research adds (QCA); the head trains, is learned or rises, in its own time after research (D124, the step's own, or the age's, D129); a price is the book's after research (QCA), an age's D129; a new unit stands on a free tile beside and takes the side's rally job; a step or an age in the queue is no person"},
 "E219": {"text": "the age (Mid's ageUp): the next age, never the hidden sixth until the peace opens it; paid at its price (D129, the ages of D130) and queued at the seat, which trains nothing else while it rises; the side's aging is its time left"},
 "E220": {"text": "the jobs (SM Gather): a villager's job is the yield it works; counts are read, not kept"},
 "E221": {"text": "QV: the find of a yield whose rate of return R is best (the walk out, the walk home and the crowd counted), of those not full (D195), not left alone for no path (D137), in the box it was sent to cut, and within the look (D197) of the point given; the straight line under-counts the walk home, so finds are weighed by it first and walked (wayLen) best first until none can beat the best"},
 "E222": {"text": "a find no path reaches, or with no spot free on its ring, is left alone a while (D137), and the next beat chooses again: one walled in tries one find a beat and waits, never every find on the map at once"},
 "E223": {"text": "assign: + sends an idle or waiting villager (else the one earning least, QV, on another job, never one posted to a field) to the yield's best find; − sets one of the job's villagers idle"},
 "E224": {"text": "the tick: training and research, ages, upkeep, the villagers, the bell"},
 "E225": {"text": "a new game: the book's stores (D172); the bell stays as Start set it"},
 "E226": {"text": "the score (QBR): what a side holds, cost ÷ D135, everything it gathered ÷ D135, and what it paid for research and ages (the ledger's research, Mid's spent) ÷ D135"},
 "E227": {"text": "First Keep v100 · combat.js (floor 10): health, the blow (QBO, QBT), the foe (QAG, QAF), nerve and the rout (QAI, QAO, QBQ), a soldier's day (its yard, kiting, healing at a shelter), squads, shapes and tempers, towers' reach (QAJ), the missile, sparks and standards. Lives alone; touches the world only through FK. A soldier's jobs: idle (at home, guarding its yard), march (to a point, fighting what it meets), hold (standing at that point), fight, rout (broken and running, or called home)"},
 "E228": {"text": "tiles from a unit to a thing: to a building's footprint, in the grid's frame"},
 "E229": {"text": "gone: pulled down (econ marks it) or dead (die marks it)"},
 "E230": {"text": "the blow's strength (Mid's dmgOf): its blow after research, blades worn by frost, rain or snow (D234, its research a share), a mounted shape's edge, its temper, its side's hunger"},
 "E231": {"text": "a blow lands (QBO); it shakes the struck one's nerve by where it comes from (QAI), sends it off by the impact (QBT), throws sparks and, from a shooter, a missile; a kill steadies the striker"},
 "E232": {"text": "QAF and QAG the foe (Mid's unitPower, groupPower, canBeat, foeValue): one its group can beat first (Lanchester: its side near summed against the foe alone, with the counters both ways), then the most harm the foe does a second for the time to kill it and reach it; wildlife picks the most worth among what bites it"},
 "E233": {"text": "the best foe in reach (Mid's bestFoe), the nearest one (nearestFoe, round any point), the nearest foe building (nearestFoeBld; the widest one's reach, D11, added to the grid's search)"},
 "E234": {"text": "to within reach of a thing, with a short search (D147)"},
 "E235": {"text": "a wave falls back to its seat, else to any building of its side"},
 "E236": {"text": "a side's wave in the field: its soldiers at the start, so nerve can be read (QBQ)"},
 "E237": {"text": "to a tile, or near one that cannot be stood on (a building's); no way there, it strikes a foe building that blocks it"},
 "E238": {"text": "QAF a group's power: each one's health × its blow (Mid's dmgOf), the blow at least D194, over D193 per, a building-only kind at D193's bonly (Mid's unitPower and powerOf, one home)"},
 "E239": {"text": "a soldier's nerve (QAI): at rest it settles back (QP), faster by its own wall or tower; outnumbered it drains; at nothing it breaks and runs (QAO), the player told once in a while"},
 "E240": {"text": "the bars: a unit's or building's health, when it is hurt and in sight; the crosshair of the player's wave"},
 "E241": {"text": "First Keep v100 · ai.js (floor 11): one brain for the computer's side, one personality (balanced). Lives alone; acts only through ECON and WAR, the same doors the menu uses. Every D.ai.beat it looks and does one round: jobs by need, people, homes, drop-offs, plots, the age, the army, the wave."},
 "E242": {"text": "the seat, and the hands it trains"},
 "E243": {"text": "the shells a side can pay for that tick a capability"},
 "E244": {"text": "each yield's camp: the drop-off that takes it in"},
 "E245": {"text": "a spot: the nearest free footprint to a point, searched in rings, kept off the home's own ring so the roads stay open"},
 "E246": {"text": "jobs by need: the yield whose share is most under its wanted share takes an idle villager, or one from the yield most over"},
 "E247": {"text": "people, homes, drop-offs, plots, the age"},
 "E248": {"text": "the army: the troop whose counters strike hardest, summed over the enemy's soldiers (Mid's bestCounter by vs), until the age's count stands"},
 "E249": {"text": "the wave: it sets out at the odds (QAF, combat.js) of D155 or better against the other side; a stalled wave goes home"},
 "E250": {"text": "First Keep v100 · sound.js (beside the stack): one player for every recipe in books/sound.js (H). Lives alone; hears the world only through FK's 'event' hook."},
 "E251": {"text": "The ear is the camera, at a height (QAX); a struck thing rings by its material (QAY); snow lowers the air's top and rain masks the quiet (QBX). No sound is typed here."},
 "E252": {"text": "each channel's volume steps, the one in use first (HX10)"},
 "E253": {"text": "a phone opens its audio only on a touch"},
 "E254": {"text": "the Ring/Silent switch silences the game; the player's music plays on (HX8)"},
 "E255": {"text": "a battle's many blows never clip a phone speaker"},
 "E256": {"text": "QAY: each mode dies with time constant tau ÷ Hz, to 80 dB down"},
 "E257": {"text": "QAX: the ear sits over the screen's middle at the height a lens of HX1's field of view needs to see the screen; a sound d along the ground is √(d² + h²) away,"},
 "E258": {"text": "full within the closest zoom's height, then falling as 1 ÷ distance (the inverse-square law in amplitude), less the air's loss"},
 "E259": {"text": "metres"},
 "E260": {"text": "QBY: a sound with a reach is full within floor × reach"},
 "E261": {"text": "the air is full: an alert never waits"},
 "E262": {"text": "thunder comes after its flash by the distance ÷ the speed of sound"},
 "E263": {"text": "QBX: rain drowns the far and quiet first"},
 "E264": {"text": "the player's volume for this channel"},
 "E265": {"text": "ambience as events: a bird from a tree in view by day, a cricket in the dark, never in winter; when one sings is a Poisson process (HX4)"},
 "E266": {"text": "QBX: the air's top falls with snow cover, on a log scale"},
 "E267": {"text": "a side's economy, fresh: its age, the steps it knows, its gathered total, the rally, and the stores' flow (this minute's in and out, the last minute's, each by reason) and the ledger of the whole game"},
 "E268": {"text": "earn and spend: every store in or out goes through these two, the one home for the stores, the minute's flow (by resource and by reason) and the ledger of where it came from and went (its words in the Words book, J1); a gain from gathering counts toward the score's wealth"},
 "E269": {"text": "what was paid comes back the way it went out: the store, the minute's spending and the ledger step back, so a cancel is as if the order never was"},
 "E270": {"text": "the stores' flow a minute: the last full minute, or before there is one the minute so far scaled up (from at least D189 seconds); net is in less out; a store's velocity runs −1 to +1 by tanh, and falling with under two minutes left is the worst there is (D189)"},
 "E271": {"text": "each minute (D188) the minute's in and out become the last minute's"},
 "E272": {"text": "the words helpers: numbers shortened (1.2k, 12k), plurals, 'a, b or c', a percent slower, a place as its lettered square, a ledger line; their words in the Words book (J), their numbers in D191"},
 "E273": {"text": "the first ending in the Words book (J5) that fits the name"},
 "E274": {"text": "how much slower a full cover of mud or snow makes a march, in percent, from its terrain factor f: 1 − 1 ÷ (1 + f) (QN)"},
 "E275": {"text": "a place as the map's lettered squares, measured from the board's corner: D190 units a square, letters across, numbers down (A1 to V22); off the board, the nearest square"},
 "E276": {"text": "a ledger line: its reasons largest first, each in its word and shortened, apart by a dot; under half a unit is left out"},
 "E277": {"text": "QCA, the effects: what each side has learned, and each side's numbers worked out once until its learning changes; a new game forgets both"},
 "E278": {"text": "a thing's keys, the names an effect may reach it by: every head of its code's letters (B, BR for BR1), its code, its ticks and a soldier's class"},
 "E279": {"text": "a number's base, from its one home: the pace (D86), a building's health (D139) or a unit's (D138), a find's or a field's rate, a price (D123, or the step's own), a step's time (its own), a unit's training (D124), a site's raising (D125), a queue's length (the mold's six, SN1), a load (D87), a home's room (D127), mud's and snow's cost (D106, how deep it sinks), studs (none), a soldier's share of a blow before armour (D228); any other key is the unit's D138 entry"},
 "E280": {"text": "the one window for a kind's number after research (QCA): flat adds first, then the boosts summed and applied once to that, then each cut on what is left (Albert, Nov 5 18:07), then the lowest kept; a price rounds each yield to the whole unit"},
 "E281": {"text": "learning a step puts its effects in force for that side; every unit and building of the side keeps its share of health as the most it can have moves"},
 "E282": {"text": "who counters whom (Mid's vsMul): the most of the striker's counters (D138 vs, its ranks' added) over the struck one's kind, class and tags; the one home the blow (QBO), the foe (QAG) and the odds (QAF) read"},
 "E283": {"text": "QAF the odds an army gives itself against a side, the one home the computers read: the counters summed both ways over the first of each army, their ratio held in D193 (Mid's matchup) bending my power"},
 "E284": {"text": "against theirs: its soldiers, its towers (not its seat) at D177 each, its people at D192 (Mid's powerFrom); the square law as odds, p² ÷ (p² + q²), which is r² ÷ (1 + r²) with r = p ÷ q"},
 "E285": {"text": "the Sides book (I) and the stances made in play, each pair's own; a new game forgets them"},
 "E286": {"text": "who belongs (the kind decides): a side's own are no group; an animal (I4) is a beast; a kind of the wild in a group's list (I3) is that group's; the rest of the wild is the Natives' (Mid's gangOf)"},
 "E287": {"text": "a stance is the pair's own, or the book's start (I2); a treaty sets it both ways between its signers only, never for a third (pacta tertiis, N159)"},
 "E288": {"text": "the one hostility test (Mid's isFoe): never one's own; an animal is everyone's foe; one of a wild group is a foe when the side is at war with that group; between sides, war"},
 "E289": {"text": "the wild looking at a side: an animal fights everyone; a group fights a side at war with it, but starts nothing with a computer (decision 4b: a camp fights a computer only once struck on its ground, which comes with the camps)"},
 "E290": {"text": "the Research book (O) by code and by key"},
 "E291": {"text": "a find's or a field's rate after the side's research (QCA): the one window, D88 or the row's own rate as the base"},
 "E292": {"text": "Mid's research lines: a line is the steps of one line at one building, in the book's order; a step waits on the one before it and on its needs (by key; a need not yet in the book is never met); the next is the first unknown step of the line"},
 "E293": {"text": "research (Mid's researchWhy and research): a step is refused when known, before its age, before its needs, already queued, with no finished building of its row, the shortest queue there full, or not paid for (the reason as a word for the menu); else paid and queued at that building; learned when it leaves the queue, its effects applied once (FK.learn)"},
 "E294": {"text": "research shows on its building (Mid's UP, PB12): the steps learned of those its row names, none, some, or half or more; a building's level (PB3, PB4, PB6): the side's age against the look's, or how many steps that raise it the side knows; the footing drawn under the walls"},
 "E295": {"text": "the keep at its level: the bastion from its points in the Sprites book (PB13)"},
 "E296": {"text": "the walked length (QBL) from a tile to beside a building: a straight step one tile, a diagonal √2; no way, infinitely far"},
 "E297": {"text": "QCI standing spots: everyone stands on a spot of its own a pace (D196) apart. A point's spots lie on the hex lattice, nearest first, rings enough for D128 people and D196's spare"},
 "E298": {"text": "a find's working ring (Mid's WORK_R, D196): as many spots as fit a pace apart round it, ⌊2π·r ÷ pace⌋ (Mid's findCap), laid on a ring wide enough that the chord between two is a pace, and clear of the ground the find keeps (D169)"},
 "E299": {"text": "spot i of c: round a find on its ring; round a building on its outline, the lane of tiles beside it, k a side, at least a pace apart, corners too, clockwise from the top-left (Mid's spotAt, in tile coordinates); round a point on the lattice; null past the last"},
 "E300": {"text": "a spot is free when its tile is walked and nobody stands on it or has claimed one within a pace less near-enough (D196); the push settles the rest"},
 "E301": {"text": "the spot u keeps at c, else the free one nearest u (round a point, the nearest the point)"},
 "E302": {"text": "walk to a spot of its own at c: the path's last tile becomes the spot itself; false when none is free or none is reached"},
 "E303": {"text": "a path's last point is reached within near-enough (D196), any point within a pace when the crowd has pushed it this step: a walker held off its way by people takes the next point"},
 "E304": {"text": "QCJ separation, neighbours only (the M3 grid): two closer than a pace part to a pace, each moved by the other's share of their mass (the Mass book, QBT's bodies), the lighter further; two on one point part along a direction fixed by their places in the roll; nobody is pushed into a tree, a wall or water"},
 "E305": {"text": "a find drawn smaller as it is used: PN1's left share and the rest by what is left (Mid's nodeScale)"},
 "E306": {"text": "the forager (QV, QX): a find takes D195's cap (a tree one feller, a field one worker) or as many as its ring has spots; the others on it crowd its rate by D195's hold; span: how far a find or a building reaches, so the straight line less both spans never over-counts the walk"},
 "E307": {"text": "QV R = c / (c/g + 2d/v + w·c/(A·v)): c the load, g the rate crowded (QX), v the walk, d the walked length to the drop-off (cached per find), w the straight walk out, A what is left up to a field's life (a tree begun counts as worth finishing); low: d by the straight line, a bound. A find with no free spot pays nothing"},
 "E308": {"text": "a lost find (Mid's decision 1): it delivers what it carries, then looks from where the find ran out within the look (D197), widening over tau; nothing found, it waits on a spot at its drop-off and looks again every few seconds, with no end; a box that is done sends it back to its work"},
 "E309": {"text": "builders who finish a place of work take it up (Mid's startWork): a field if nobody works it; a camp (a drop-off that takes fewer than every yield) sends them to the best find it takes"},
 "E310": {"text": "a box over finds (Mid's boxCut): n villagers, idle first then the nearest, cut the finds in it, from the nearest open one outside when none inside is open, then go back to the work they left; Send out: the last villager on a field goes idle; posted: on a field; idlePost: a finished field nobody works"},
 "E311": {"text": "a trained unit steps out onto the free spot of its building's outline nearest the middle (Mid's stepOut); none free, the queue waits; with your rally flag up, a soldier marches to it (Mid's rally0, F21)"},
 "E312": {"text": "nudged off its spot, it gives way while pushed and steps back once the crowd lets go: no tug of war with a walker, no shuffle between two on their spots (a push moves each less than near-enough)"},
 "E313": {"text": "how many of a building a side may have now: its age's limit with research added (D199), none before its age (D200); why not, in Mid's words (capWhy)"},
 "E314": {"text": "why a building may not stand here, Mid's rules in order: the edge, the limit, the ground under it (a gate may take its owner's wall piece), two squares from every building unless one is a wall, gate or field, and never touching one that trains (canPlace)"},
 "E315": {"text": "two squares from every find too, measured from the footprint's edge to the find's middle (Mid's nodesNear)"},
 "E316": {"text": "the ghost snaps to the nearest spot that fits beside one of yours (touching, or a lane apart, edges or middles in line) or in line with one farther off; else it stays where the finger is (Mid's snapGhost)"},
 "E317": {"text": "taking a building down pays back half its price, all of it early in the build; its line is paid back in full first (Mid's shellBack, refundOf, demolish)"},
 "E318": {"text": "a wall dragged from corner to corner: a straight run of tiles, four-connected so nothing slips through a diagonal (Mid's wallLine); laid piece by piece while the stores last, each sent a builder; the seal is a foe's walk out from the Town Center over the tiles not yet built too (Mid's sealPath, by v100's A*)"},
 "E319": {"text": "the walk starts on the Town Center's own floor; walls being laid count as built; everything is put back after"},
 "E320": {"text": "a builder remembers the work it left (its find and yield, and whether it was pulled off it) so it can go back (Mid's sendBuilder); one already beside the site stops the walk it was on, so its arrival cannot turn it back to that walk's work"},
 "E321": {"text": "a new site gets the nearest free villager; with none free, your nearest worker is pulled off and goes back after, a computer's lowest earner keeps building (Mid's autoBuilder and pickVil); a line of wall gets two at most, who work down it"},
 "E322": {"text": "back to the very find it left if it still stands, else the best of its yield, else idle (Mid's backToWork)"},
 "E323": {"text": "the next site for a builder done: a wall piece close by, else a site nobody raises (Mid's repairTick)"},
 "E324": {"text": "a site finished: a drop-off or field puts its builder to work there, unless it was pulled off other work; else the next site, else back to work"},
 "E325": {"text": "mending, Mid's: three times the build time for a whole building, a quarter of its price paid as it goes; short of any part, it stops (QCK)"},
 "E326": {"text": "a crew of n raises a site at n^0.7 (QAC), counted once a tick; frost slows stone work; the site's health rises with it"},
 "E327": {"text": "of the buildings that can take an order, the one with the shortest line (Mid's shortest)"},
 "E328": {"text": "a gate is walkable only to those its owner does not count a foe: asked of combat.js by the shut hook, for the walker on the path in hand; none in hand, it is shut"},
 "E329": {"text": "a gate is shut to a foe of its owner, and to an unknown walker (the seal's foe)"},
 "E330": {"text": "the computer's wall ring: from its age, with stone, a few pieces a round, gates first, while it keeps its stone (Mid's decide)"},
 "E331": {"text": "an arc of wall round the Town Center facing the middle, four-connected; its two squares nearest the middle are the gate (Mid's wallPlan)"},
 "E332": {"text": "who trains a kind: the building with the shortest line; walls are laid as lines; walls and gates show the seal"},
 "E333": {"text": "the ghost to the finger, lifted above it on a phone, snapped beside yours; the reason it may not stand is kept for the label"},
 "E334": {"text": "a wall's next corner snaps flat or upright when nearly so; its tiles from its corners (Mid's wallSnap, wallSet)"},
 "E335": {"text": "a finger on a wall's corner moves it, on its line slides the whole wall; elsewhere it looks around and a tap adds a corner (Mid's wallHit, wallDrag)"},
 "E336": {"text": "Build: a wall line laid while the stores last, said in one toast; a building sent its nearest free villager (or the one picked), then the ghost waits on the next spot beside it until the limit or the purse says no (Mid's commitPlace)"},
 "E337": {"text": "while placing, the finger moves the ghost (a wall's corner or line), not the map"},
 "E338": {"text": "the ghost's own art tinted green where it fits and red where not, one tinted copy a sprite and colour (Mid's ghostTint)"},
 "E339": {"text": "while a wall or gate is placed: a red line where a foe could walk in, or Sealed over the Town Center (Mid's drawSeal)"},
 "E340": {"text": "the ghost: a wall's tiles green or red with its corners, the first ringed green; a building's guides to yours in line and its tinted art, no footprint box (Mid's drawGhost, drawGuides)"},
 "E341": {"text": "a tap on open ground while the Build page is open: what fits there is picked and its ghost put there (Mid's suggestAt)"},
 "E342": {"text": "dragging the ghost near the screen's edge scrolls the map (Mid's edgeScroll)"},
 "E343": {"text": "what fits a spot: a drop-off for finds far from theirs, more of what stands round you, a wall in a narrow way (a gate beside your wall), a home when room is short; the best score wins (Mid's suggestAt)"},
 "E344": {"text": "fish round every lake: a spot every D218 per of its radius, walked out from the middle to the shore and set inset back into the water, each holding its share of the lake (Mid's layFish)"},
 "E345": {"text": "a find laid where something falls (game becomes a carcass where it stood); a lake near enough to stand a dock by, past its beach"},
 "E346": {"text": "a boar near every Town Center, at the book's spot in each corner (Mid's boar)"},
 "E347": {"text": "the gather beat: the field is worked now (its soil wears); a flock's food goes straight to the store; a plot with an amount runs down and its worker waits by it when it is cut out (Mid's replant wait); a famine weakens the work (hungerOf)"},
 "E348": {"text": "what a unit eats a second: its kind's shares (its Upkeep, with research) of a person's day; a famine past its grace weakens work and blows (Mid's shareOf, hungerOf); fish are worked only near a finished dock of the side (Mid's dockNear); food in reach is any find, field of one's own or game (Mid's foodInReach)"},
 "E349": {"text": "everyone eats, every moment: a villager working food eats from its find, not the store (a field and game for nothing, a shepherd from the store); the store empty is hunger, and with no food in reach a famine, timed from its start (Mid's upkeepTick, starveTick)"},
 "E350": {"text": "an order of yours costs its soldiers' meals for D213's seconds, never more than the store holds (Mid's orderCost; the tiredness comes with the charge)"},
 "E351": {"text": "the year's work: everyone eats; a field's soil wears while worked and rests back, never under its floor (QAA, Mid's natureTick); each season's turn once"},
 "E352": {"text": "each season's turn: food in store spoils (QAD); in spring fish regrow (QY), lambs come (QY) and a tended flock is culled to half for mutton (QZ); wolves near a pasture take sheep every season; the harvest of the year is rolled in spring (Mid's seasonTurn)"},
 "E353": {"text": "a cut-out plot is replanted at D222's share of its price and is full again; from a drop-off, every cut-out plot of what it takes, nearest first, as many as can be paid for (Mid's replantWhy, replant, cutOut, replantAll)"},
 "E354": {"text": "send a hunter: the given villager, or the nearest idle one, else the nearest from other work (not a builder or a posted worker); it fights the game (Mid's sendHunt)"},
 "E355": {"text": "QBO the blow on a unit: × the counter; a villager's javelin on game × D221; on a soldier, an animal's at D231 wild, a runner's × routHit, × its armour share (D228), its shape's hit and against riders, from behind a blade × D141; roofed against missiles; on a building × the striker's bld (Mid's hurt)"},
 "E356": {"text": "a building that falls pays its destroyer D233 of its price (Mid's plunderBld); game falls as a carcass of its meat where it stood, and its hunters butcher it (Mid's kill)"},
 "E357": {"text": "hunt a beast from its card; replant a cut-out plot, or every one a drop-off takes, from theirs"},
 "E358": {"text": "a pasture's card counts its sheep"},
 "E359": {"text": "the town is told what food, the seasons and the flock do, in the Words book's news"},
 "E360": {"text": "the ground under a walker as it steps toward the tile to (QN, QR): its mud (the marsh always), its snow cover, its ice (D225), the friction its step needs by what steps (G9), what the ground offers off the ice (dry to mud to snow) and on it (G8 by the air, melting to hard; the studs' G10 if iron bites), the grade up to it, and which way it walks against the wind"},
 "E361": {"text": "QCB the pace: Pandolf's cost of walking solved for the speed, its power set by the walker's base (D86 with research, QCA) unloaded on flat firm ground in still air; the load, the ground's η, the grade and the wind change it; × each state (D224) and, after a slip, the shortened step on its share of ice (QR)"},
 "E362": {"text": "QR each second on ice: the step lands on the ice with the chance of its cover, else on the ground; it slips exactly when the friction it needs is more than that ground offers, and walks on wary (a shorter step) until it is off the ice"},
 "E363": {"text": "a slipped walker stands G10's seconds; which way it walks, for the wind"},
 "E364": {"text": "above freezing lake ice's degree-seconds fall four times as fast; ground ice thaws by the degree (D225) and its degree-seconds are set to match what is left"},
 "E365": {"text": "the share of the ground under ice: √ of its freezing degree-seconds over D225's full (QQ, Stefan)"},
 "E366": {"text": "the armour kit a side has learned (Mid's KIT): 0 to 3 steps of the Sprites book's kit, each turning a person's slots (mail and a steel helm, then plate, the great helm, its crest and a cape in the figure's own colours), with a shoulder guard of leather, mail or steel"},
 "E367": {"text": "one drawing list for every figure that is not a person or a beast (the engines, the chariot, the elephant, the riders, the elite pennant): each part a brush (P, E, L, Q, rect, wheel, planks, helm, horse, person), in a frame moved and turned (at), or drawn only in the blow's frame (atk) or out of it (rest); a value may sway with the stride or change in the blow's frame. The numbers live in the Sprites book"},
 "E368": {"text": "a look by its rank: level 0 the look itself, level n the nth of its rank list, past the list its last (Mid's LOOKS by tier)"},
 "E369": {"text": "the Unit shell's classes: a class's kinds in book order; what a building trains (D133: a shell, or a class's kinds); a kind is open from its age (D130)"},
 "E370": {"text": "a kind's ranks (Mid's tiers): the steps whose rank names it, learned, in book order, give its level and its name; the kit is how many armour steps a soldier's side has learned"},
 "E371": {"text": "the army's ceiling: soldiers (a kind with a class), queued ones counted, against D226 (Mid's ARMYMAX; a fallen side's share, capA, joins it with M30)"},
 "E372": {"text": "the army: a side's soldiers, the kinds with a class (Mid's armyOf); BUSY names who keeps to its own work and armyFree leaves them out (the routed now; the spy, the shrine, the escort and the school with their modules)"},
 "E373": {"text": "why a kind waits: the age it opens in (Mid's trainWhy)"},
 "E374": {"text": "the load, the ground's η (QN, research cuts), and the wind's drag ½ρCdA v|v| (W1, by the mass to the ⅔, D224), v the walk against the wind (Pugh)"},
 "E375": {"text": "aV² + bV + c = 0: a the walking term, b the grade and the wind as a grade (100F ÷ g), c the standing and load terms less the walker's power; the positive root"},
 "E376": {"text": "QCL the weather of the moment: rates, wind and visibility from the strengths; the wind signed and gusting; a blizzard's hours counted while its three conditions hold, and the flag at the NWS's three hours"},
 "E377": {"text": "the weather's book (D229), a game hour, the gusts (a fractal of the day's dice, set at the start) and the particle pool (the looks' dice)"},
 "E378": {"text": "QCL rain and snow rates, the wind, its gusts and the visibility (QK: Koschmieder over rain's and snow's extinction); a blizzard by the NWS: snow, wind or gusts at 35 mph or more, visibility under a quarter mile"},
 "E379": {"text": "rain: Marshall–Palmer sizes at the rate (λ = N0 R^exp), each drop falling at its size's speed in metres a second on the screen, carried and slanted by the wind"},
 "E380": {"text": "snow: flakes falling slow to fast by size, carried by the wind and swaying"},
 "E381": {"text": "the white of low visibility: the contrast lost over the screen's width, 1 − e^(−3.912 d ÷ V) (QK)"},
 "E382": {"text": "a side knows a step of research by its key"},
 "E383": {"text": "the player's three squads (Mid's battalions): each one's plan by class, its shape, temper and intent (the dials), and the one picked for orders (none: the whole army); the computers keep Guard and the line"},
 "E384": {"text": "who is in which squad (Mid's rebattalion): each keeps its squad while its class has room in the plan, the rest fill the first squad with room; none before Battalions"},
 "E385": {"text": "a squad's plan by class (Mid's sqPlan): a step of one under ten, five above, the whole squad at most D227"},
 "E386": {"text": "what a squad lacks, by kind to train (Mid's musterGap): its plan less its soldiers and those mustering for it, each class as its first kind of the age"},
 "E387": {"text": "where a blow comes from (Mid's fromWhere): the cosine between the line's facing (its own and its comrades' near, D232) and the striker; the front whenever it can turn to meet it or a comrade covers that side"},
 "E388": {"text": "QAI a loss drains each soldier of its side within D231's lossR by 1 ÷ (D142 × n) (Mid's died, Dupuy's break)"},
 "E389": {"text": "Lanchester's odds above a half is exactly the ratio above one"},
 "E390": {"text": "a soldier at home keeps to its yard: within D235 of its post or of its Town Center (Mid's nearHome)"},
 "E391": {"text": "a foe building in the way is struck (Mid's findBlocker)"},
 "E392": {"text": "a group dressed into its shape at a tile (Mid's formUp): facing from home to there, the squads in order, blades before shooters; a column three files, a square √n, a front one rank, a choke three, a line about twice as wide as deep, a wedge point first, support a ring of blades round the shooters; each walks to its own place, at the pace of the slowest that is not an engine; a drill (the War Director's) keeps the shape for its time"},
 "E393": {"text": "Albert's x% by x%: a soldier in a drill not D242's share of the way to its place by that share of the time stands where it is (Mid's drillOn, drillHold)"},
 "E394": {"text": "at home an army stands in the yard of the building that trained it (or its Town Center), toward the map's middle, a block a squad side by side, blades in front, shooters behind (Mid's formUp, homeSpot)"},
 "E395": {"text": "a broken soldier runs D231's run a step from the nearest foe (or toward home) at its own pace, for the run's seconds (research shortens it), then comes back at D231's after (Mid's routSecs)"},
 "E396": {"text": "a soldier's day (Mid's solTick): nerve, healing by a shelter (QP), its drill; it keeps its foe while in reach of its sight × D238 leash × its temper's chase; it looks for the best foe and keeps the one it has unless the new is D132 better or the old is at its blade; at home only near its yard; No pursuit and Buildings first; Hold fights only what comes within reach; a march arrived holds; at home it walks back to its post"},
 "E397": {"text": "QAJ the missile: projectile motion with quadratic drag (the arrow's, W10), loosed at D245's angle, stepped until it lands; its speed for a distance found by halving; a tower reaches as far as the arrow that lands at its bow's ground reach would land from its height, plus its research"},
 "E398": {"text": "in reach: it faces its foe; a shooter reloading with a blade near steps back (Mid's KITE), then strikes when ready"},
 "E399": {"text": "the missiles in flight: a streak along the drag path, its tail D245's share of the flight"},
 "E400": {"text": "a blow's sparks (Mid's sparkDraw)"},
 "E401": {"text": "the standards (Mid's drawStandards): a group of D sprites' least on the move carries its side's flag, a ring at its foot as full as its health"},
 "E402": {"text": "Muster (Mid's musterN, musterCost, musterWhy, muster): a squad's lack in one order at the War Council: D244's times the price, the slowest kind's time shared by the buildings that train it × D244's time; refused without the step, with nothing lacking, without a council, a kind's building, room in the army or the town, or the price (a reason as a word for the menu); it comes out together into its squad"},
 "E403": {"text": "the squads: a tap picks one for orders, a tap on the one picked opens its dials; Set up opens them for the one picked or the whole army"},
 "E404": {"text": "the squads' words and the step each dial waits for (Engagement, Formations, Battalions)"},
 "E405": {"text": "the War Council's card: the three squads, the picked one's plan by class (− and +) and Muster for what it lacks"},
 "E406": {"text": "the orders, missions and the War Director's measures and words; the groups on the march (ORD), the missions by squad or the whole army (MS), and the moves' waits (AT)"},
 "E407": {"text": "the archers' arc (Mid's dress 'arc'): each on a circle of the arc's radius round the foe, a rank's gap apart along it, facing in"},
 "E408": {"text": "a charge spent: the pace drops to D249 slow and settles back to the walker's own (QP, N16); while it lasts the pace is D249 spd times the charge's research"},
 "E409": {"text": "the orders' shared measures: a point of a tile, the tile of a point, the length between, a group's centre, a tile's straight steps"},
 "E410": {"text": "the walk over the straight line (Mid's routeK): the way by A* (QBL), its steps summed, held within D247 least and route"},
 "E411": {"text": "a group's order you can follow (Mid's march): its tile, label, start and walk ratio; each soldier carries it, and the player hears where they march"},
 "E412": {"text": "each soldier's one word (Mid's armyStatus): rout, fight, rally (sent home, walking to the flag, or away from its place), march, or hold once still for D247 still"},
 "E413": {"text": "the obvious order for what is picked (Mid's order, Albert Nov 2): a foe is fought, a beast hunted, a site raised or mended, a field or camp worked, a find gathered, the ground walked, each villager to its own spot; a side not at war is refused"},
 "E414": {"text": "missions: a mission's soldiers, the hostile soldiers a group sees near it, and the chance (QAF) of the group against them with the counters both ways"},
 "E415": {"text": "each beat: every order's centre, count, fight and time left, arrived once all have stopped (Mid's ordersTick); every mission goes, acts or is done, its chance eased, lost or losing said once (Mid's missionsTick)"},
 "E416": {"text": "Go (Mid's hudFire, hudGo): a squad's idle soldiers, else the army's, march on the crosshair as one order and one mission; every ready squad goes, else the army"},
 "E417": {"text": "who can still reach a fight in time, fastest first, until the fight is even (Mid's reinforcePlan); grouped into waves by arrival"},
 "E418": {"text": "the War Director: the soldiers of a kind that can go, the crosshair's tile, a move's wait in seconds; the charge's reason, the charge, fall back in order"},
 "E419": {"text": "the Director's six moves and the bombard (Mid's DIRECTS): each returns what it says, a reason without its bang when nobody moved"},
 "E420": {"text": "a kind's move, tap or hold (Mid's direct): it says its word, pays its meals (D213) and sounds its event"},
 "E421": {"text": "the choke (Mid's chokeAt): a drag across a gap, the soldiers stand in it as many files as it holds, facing the foe seen, else away from home; a standing order"},
 "E422": {"text": "the nearest cover (Mid's coverNear): an open tile with forest within D252 cover, within D252 find of the crosshair"},
 "E423": {"text": "an ambush in place (Mid's ambushTick): once there it goes to ground (no foe sees it); a foe within reach or a blow springs them all with a charge"},
 "E424": {"text": "your groups on the march (Mid's drawOrders): a dashed line to where they go, a ring there, the time left; the rally flag (flagAt); leaves over a hidden soldier (leavesOver)"},
 "E425": {"text": "the finger's gesture: where it went down and is, when, and what a module made of it (a line, the crosshair, a box); a hold after D246 hold"},
 "E426": {"text": "the hold's ring once the finger plainly holds, and the box being drawn (Mid's drawTouch)"},
 "E427": {"text": "Attack is Go, held it is Home (Mid's station); the rally flag, held the ambush; the choke tool; reinforce the mission most in need; a kind's two moves; the quick action's sword and close"},
 "E428": {"text": "a button held for D246 hold runs its second verb, and its click is swallowed (Mid's lpT)"},
 "E429": {"text": "Albert's one rule for the finger (Build 40, Nov 2): a tap picks yours, a second tap opens the card; with yours picked a tap is the obvious order; on open ground with nothing picked, the sword and close (Nov 3); a group's ring picks the group; a cut-out plot replants"},
 "E430": {"text": "the crosshair (Mid's aimSpot, aimColor): a foe, a find or the ground under the tap; green yours, red a foe or a hostile near, blue an ally, white nature"},
 "E431": {"text": "the finger's holds and drags on the map: the choke drawn, the crosshair dragged, yours picked to keep picking, a box picks yours in it"},
 "E432": {"text": "the choke being drawn and the crosshair (Mid's drawReticle): brackets, a sonar ring, turning chevrons, a scan line, the cross, the time and the square"},
 "E433": {"text": "a tile on the board (the floor gives -1 off it)"},
 "E434": {"text": "the narrowest gap on the road to a foe (Mid's gapOnRoad): from D251 ai.from tiles out to half way, each ai.step tiles, the open width across the road, the narrowest of ai.min to ai.max"},
 "E435": {"text": "the computer holds a gap (Mid's chokeClaim): once each D251 ai.every, with enough idle foot, files deep across the narrowest gap on the road to its nearest foe, for ai.hold"}
});
